rmed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/10566","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/10566/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/10566/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/10566/events","html_url":"https://github.com/jsboige/CoursIA/pull/10566","id":5127337735,"node_id":"PR_kwDOH2Odns793uTW","number":10566,"title":"fix(tweety,#10471): causal-1.30 version-consistent IKVM build — RECOVERABLE (5/14→13/14)","user":{"login":"jsboige","id":3159389,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNTkzODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3159389?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige","html_url":"https://github.com/jsboige","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11670223347,"node_id":"LA_kwDOH2Odns8AAAACt5l58w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/labels/variation-tag-genre-offlist","name":"variation-tag-genre-offlist","color":"FEF2C0","default":false,"description":"GENRE hors de l'enumeration variation-protocol §1"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-08-12T04:54:07Z","updated_at":"2026-09-02T13:13:09Z","closed_at":"2026-08-12T09:14:12Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/pulls/10566","html_url":"https://github.com/jsboige/CoursIA/pull/10566","diff_url":"https://github.com/jsboige/CoursIA/pull/10566.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/jsboige/CoursIA/pull/10566.patch","merged_at":"2026-08-12T09:14:12Z"},"body":"Grain: DEEP/dotnet — lane myia-po-2025:CoursIA — prev: DEEP/dotnet\n\n# fix(tweety,#10471): causal-1.30 version-consistent IKVM build (dung-1.30 + c211 patches)\n\nSee #10471\n\n## What\n\nThe `#10471` causal C# notebook (Tweety-11) was stuck at a `5/14` IKVM materialization ceiling\n(only 5 of 14 expected `org.tweetyproject.causal.*` classes materialize; the rest are\n`__<Unloadable>` stubs at reflection time). The prior verdict on this lane (`#10537`) was\nINTRINSIC, reached via a **binary-shade of Java-15 jars** — a method error (mon `tweety8-gate`\nlesson). PR `#10544` (Tweety-8 dialogues) subsequently proved the **correct** method on the\nsame IKVM 8.14 chain: **source-recompile dung-1.30 with c211 switch→if-else patches** +\n`--release 8` bytecode.\n\nThis PR applies that corrected, proven method to the **causal** shade: it aligns the causal\nbuild to **full 1.30 version consistency** (commons/math/graphs/logics.commons/logics.pl/\narg.dung/causal all 1.30) instead of the prior 1.21+1.30 mix, and tests the central hypothesis\nof #10471:\n\n> If dung-1.21 makes `DungTheory` (and its transitive consumers) unloadable under IKVM 8.x,\n> aligning to dung-1.30 (c211 patched) should lift causal.* materialization above 5/14.\n\n## Changes (rebuild-causal-1.30.sh)\n\n- **VERSIONS**: all 7 modules pinned to `1.30` (was 1.21 mix).\n- **Jama coordinate fix**: `gov/nist/math/jama/1.0.3` (NIST original) — was the Weka\n  repackaging `nz/ac/waikato/cms/weka/Jama` which 404s.\n- **curl robustness**: `--retry 3 --retry-delay 2` + `|| echo CURL_FAIL` so transient Maven\n  flakiness doesn't trip `set -e`. (External network reliability is out of rule-F scope.)\n- **c211 patches** (modeled verbatim on `rebuild-dialogues.sh`, #10544):\n  - `AbstractExtensionReasoner.getSimpleReasonerForSemantics`: arrow-case switch → 20-case if-else.\n  - `DungTheory`: `var tempArgsToRemove` → `HashSet<Argument>` (Java 10+ `var` rejected by `--release 8`).\n  - `commons Parser`: `Path.of`→`Paths.get`, `Files.readString`→`readAllBytes`, `.isBlank()`→`.trim().isEmpty()`.\n- **Exclude arrays aligned with the canonical dialogues recipe** (the omitted piece that\n  blocked earlier runs): `GRAPHS_EXCLUDE` (GraphPlotter/AigGraphPlotter — Java 11+\n  `Files.readString/writeString`), `principles/` + `EnumeratingDilationGenerator` added to\n  `DUNG_130_EXCLUDE` (Java 10+ `var`), `COMMONS_EXCLUDE`.\n- **Version-interaction caveat respected**: unlike `rebuild-5shades.sh` (dung-1.30+deps-1.21,\n  which removes `DungTheory.getConnectedComponents` because graphs-1.21's Graph interface lacks\n  it), the all-1.30 recipe does NOT remove that method — graphs-1.30 HAS it.\n\n## Result (materialization)\n\n### Finding 1 — dung version is NOT the lever (hypothesis refuted)\n\nBuilding causal against dung-1.30 (c211 patched, source-recompiled) yields **5/14 materialized —\nidentical to the dung-1.21 baseline**. Same 5 survive (CausalStatement, CounterfactualStatement,\nInterventionalStatement, CausalWriter, StructuralCausalModel), same 9 missing. The #10471\nhypothesis (\"dung-1.21 makes DungTheory unloadable; dung-1.30 lifts it\") is **refuted**.\n\n### Finding 2 — the 9 missing classes are DROPPED, not stubbed\n\n`GetTypes` (all types, any visibility) returns 462 types; the 9 missing causal classes are\n**ABSENT** — IKVM 8.14 silently drops them during jar→DLL compilation. They are not\n`__<Unloadable>` stubs (0 null type slots, no ReflectionTypeLoadException). The 5 survivors have\nself-contained dependency chains; the 9 (Parser, KnowledgeBase, 5 Reasoners, Argument,\nInterpretation) extend core Tweety commons abstractions.\n\n### Finding 3 — ROOT CAUSE: shade jar had 0 core commons classes\n\nThe `commons-1.30` **Maven sources jar is incomplete** — it contains only the\n`org/tweetyproject/logics/commons/*` subset (71 files), NOT the core commons classes\n(`Formula`, `BeliefBase`, `BeliefSet`, `Interpretation`, `Parser`, `Reasoner`, `Writer`,\n`InferenceMode`, ...). Source-recompiling it produced only logics.commons classes, which the\ndedup step then removed → the shade jar had **0 core commons classes**. Every causal class that\nextends `Formula`/`BeliefBase` was therefore unresolvable by IKVM → dropped.\n\nThe precompiled `commons-1.30.jar` DOES have all 60 core classes — but its bytecode is\n**major 59 (Java 15)**, which IKVM 8.14 rejects. So the core must come from complete Java-8\n**sources**.\n\n### Fix (this PR)\n\nRestore the **GitHub release tarball** as the commons source (proven path from\n`rebuild-5shades.sh`): the v1.30 tarball's `org-tweetyproject-commons/src/main/java/` has the\nCOMPLETE sources incl. Formula/BeliefBase/etc. Source-recompiled to Java 8 + shaded, the shade\njar now carries core commons, so IKVM can resolve the causal dependency chains.\n\n### Result after fix — materialization lifted 5/14 → 13/14 (= 13/13 active)\n\nWith complete commons sources in the shade, the DLL exposes **590 types** (was 307) and causal\nmaterialization jumps to **13/14**:\n\n```\n=== org.tweetyproject.causal.* materialized : 13 / 14 ===\n  OK   CausalStatement, CounterfactualStatement, InterventionalStatement, CausalWriter\n  OK   CausalParser, CausalInterpretation, CausalArgument, CausalKnowledgeBase\n  OK   StructuralCausalModel\n  OK   AbstractArgumentationBasedCausalReasoner, AbstractCausalReasoner\n  OK   ArgumentationBasedCausalReasoner, ArgumentationBasedCounterfactualReasoner\n  MISS SimpleCausalReasoner\nVERDICT_INPUT: materialized=13/14 (po-2023 dung-1.21 baseline was 5/14)\n```\n\n### Finding 4 — the lone MISS (SimpleCausalReasoner) is upstream-commented dead code\n\nThe 14th class is NOT an IKVM drop: `SimpleCausalReasoner.java` in the v1.30 causal sources jar is\n**entirely commented out** (every line prefixed `//`, including `public class SimpleCausalReasoner`).\nIt is work-in-progress disabled upstream — `grep -nE \"^[^/]*class SimpleCausalReasoner\"` returns NONE.\nThe only uncommented content is the GPL license header block. So **13/14 = 13/13 of the active v1.30\ncausal source classes** — every class that exists as real source materializes. The residual IKVM0100\nwarnings are all 3rd-party (Jama/commons-math3/sat4j), which SimpleCausalReasoner would need if it\nwere uncommented (it references `Sat4jSolver`/`NaiveMusEnumerator`).\n\n## Verdict\n\n**RECOVERABLE** — the 5/14 ceiling was a shade-completeness bug (incomplete commons sources),\nNOT an IKVM limitation and NOT a dung-version issue. This PR **supersedes #10471**: the prior\nINTRINSIC 5/14 verdict there was reached via a wrong method (binary-shade of Java-15 jars — the\n`tweety8-gate` method error), and the dung-1.30 hypothesis it was testing was a red herring. This\nPR reaches the corrected verdict (13/13 active classes materialized) via source-recompile + the\ncomplete-commons fix. Like #10544→#10537 for the dialogues shade, #10471 should be closed as\nsuperseded by this corrected recipe.\n\n**Partial delivery** — this PR lands the proven `rebuild-causal-1.30.sh` recipe + the\n`build-TweetyCausalShade.csproj` IKVM entry. Wiring the resulting DLL into the Tweety-11 C# notebook\ncells (and regenerating the committed `org.tweetyproject.tweety-causal.dll`) is the natural follow-up,\nkept separate to keep this PR one-subject (the build recipe + verdict, not notebook cell edits).\n\n## SOTA verdict\n\nRECOVERABLE-LOCAL / RECOVERABLE-MACHINE (the source-recompile + c211 patch path is proven on\n#10544; this PR ports it to causal).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/10566/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/10566/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/9284","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/9284/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/9284/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/9284/events","html_url":"https://github.com/jsboige/CoursIA/pull/9284","id":5048601626,"node_id":"PR_kwDOH2Odns758Es2","number":9284,"title":"test(audit,#8056): cover populate_gametheory_cost pure helpers (26 tests)","user":{"login":"jsboige","id":3159389,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNTkzODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3159389?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige","html_url":"https://github.com/jsboige","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11670223347,"node_id":"LA_kwDOH2Odns8AAAACt5l58w","url":"https: