wired via #10544; this closes a second of the four.\n\n## The breakthrough chain (this session)\n\n1. **#10566** (prior cycle, DEEP/dotnet): proved the causal shade DLL materializes **13/13 active classes** (was stuck at 5/14 \"INTRINSIC\"). Root cause was an incomplete commons sources jar, fixed via the GitHub tarball.\n2. **Loading spike** (this cycle): the 8.14.0-built DLL **loads under the IKVM 8.15.0 runtime** (forward-compat — no rebuild needed). 6/7 key causal types resolve, `StructuralCausalModel` constructs.\n3. **This PR** (DEEP/notebook-dotnet): ports the proven loading recipe into the notebook + a Sprinkler SCM demo.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **§6 \"Parité jpype ⇔ IKVM\"** added to `Tweety-11-Causal-Csharp.ipynb` (4 cells: markdown intro, IKVM bootstrap+load, Sprinkler demo, interpretation). Exercises renumbered §6→§7.\n- **`org.tweetyproject.tweety-causal.dll`** committed (shade IKVM 8.15, 914 Ko, 13/13 active causal classes — built via the #10566 `rebuild-causal-1.30.sh` recipe). Established pattern: 16 sibling DLLs already live in `Tweety/`.\n\nThe section is **additive** — the from-scratch engine (§1–5) is untouched, per #10381 (\"L'effort from-scratch n'est pas en cause et ne doit pas être retiré\"). All from-scratch cell outputs are preserved byte-identical.\n\n## Result (real execution)\n\nExecuted end-to-end via the `.net-csharp` kernel (dotnet-interactive): **14/14 code cells, 0 errors**. The IKVM demo cell produces:\n\n```\n=== Réseau Sprinkler — moteur TweetyProject (IKVM) ===\nBackground atoms: [cloudy]\nStructural Equations:\nsprinkler <=> cloudy\nwet <=> sprinkler||rain\nrain <=> cloudy\n\n=== Après do(sprinkler=True) — chirurgie causale ===\nsprinkler <=> +          ← surgery: sprinkler disconnected from cloudy\nwet <=> sprinkler||rain\nrain <=> cloudy\n```\n\n**Parity confirmed**: `do(sprinkler=True)` replaces `sprinkler <=> cloudy` with `sprinkler <=> +` (constant) — the **identical** do-calculus surgery the from-scratch §3 teaches (`do(drops=True)` → `drops <=> +`). The real Java engine and the from-scratch C# engine agree.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `validate_pr_notebooks.py`: **PASS** (14 cells, .net-csharp, 0 leak, 0 C.1).\n- All code cells: `execution_count != null` + coherent outputs.\n- **0 leak**: probe-address banner stripped (9 lines, `strip_probe_banner.py`); papermill `input/output_path` normalized to basename. DLL binary scanned — no machine paths.\n- `detect_markdown_rendering.py`: 0 violations.\n- From-scratch §4 Sprinkler / §2 reasoner outputs verified **byte-identical** to origin/main (no re-exec churn — the diff is purely additive + the IKVM section).\n\n## Scope (partial)\n\nThis PR wires **Tweety-11** only. Tweety-6 and 7a remain (separate grains). `See #10381` (the Epic stays open until all 4 are wired + the series publishes). The natural follow-up: the `ArgumentationBasedCausalReasoner` (SAT-based, needs sat4j) for full query parity — out of scope here (the SCM + do-calculus + twin-network demo is the pedagogically sufficient parity proof).\n\n## SOTA verdict\n\n**SOTA-OK** — the real TweetyProject Java causal engine is invoked via IKVM (not a from-scratch toy, not an ASCII workaround). The do-calculus surgery output is the genuine Java `StructuralCausalModel.intervene()` result.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/10570/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/10570/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/8973","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/8973/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/C