ige/CoursIA/pull/8973","diff_url":"https://github.com/jsboige/CoursIA/pull/8973.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/jsboige/CoursIA/pull/8973.patch","merged_at":"2026-07-31T18:39:42Z"},"body":"Grain: MED/data — lane myia-po-2023:CoursIA — prev: MED/tooling #8972 (CLEAN/MERGEABLE) · MED/qc #8966 (MERGED)\n\nResidual of **#8955**: the 34th cost-divergent notebook — the only **non-QC**\none — `hmm_alpha_research.ipynb` (ML-Training). This is **my own flagged\nresidual** from #8966 (I excluded it rather than risk a regression on\nML-Training turf).\n\n## The defect (#8955, firsthand on origin/main `2d0858f1d`)\n\nSame regression class as the 23 QC quantbooks fixed by #8966: the `metadata.cost`\nscan-skeleton (dated **2026-07-29**) flattened the **curated** cell#0 frontmatter\ncost (dated **2026-07-23**, 6 days earlier):\n\n| field | frontmatter (curated) | metadata.cost (skeleton) | after this PR |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `cpu_min` | **90** (27-cell research notebook) | 8 (flat default) | **90** |\n| `reproducibility` | **MEDIUM** | HIGH (flat) | **MEDIUM** |\n| `free_alternative` | null | \"self\" | null |\n| `metadata_written` | 2026-07-23T01:30Z | 2026-07-29 | 2026-07-23T01:30Z |\n\n`_cost_equivalent` flagged `[cpu_min, reproducibility]`.\n\n## Why #8966's script skipped it (the malformed frontmatter)\n\n`migrate_cost_frontmatter_to_metadata.py` returned `skip-already-migrated`\nbecause `parse_frontmatter` returned `None`: the cell#0 frontmatter is\n**malformed** — it opens with `---` but is **never closed by a `---`** (a blank\nline then the `# H1` follow directly). The `_FRONTMATTER_RE` regex over-matches\ninto the prose (up to the first section `---` divider), `yaml.safe_load` fails\non the mixed YAML+markdown, and the parser bails. Migrated **one-shot**\n(extending the parser for malformed YAML would be disproportionate for 1\nnotebook; documented here for recurrence).\n\n## The fix\n\n`merged = {**metadata_cost, **frontmatter_cost}` (frontmatter wins on overlap;\nmetadata keeps `notes`, `qcc_tokens_est`, `vram_*`, `gpu_min`), then strip the\nmalformed frontmatter block (lines 1–14 + trailing blank), leaving the H1 to\nstart cell#0. `metadata.cost` carries the curated values; `metadata_written`\nrefreshes to the curated timestamp.\n\n## Verification (firsthand, all canonical tools post-apply)\n\n- **byte_stable_baseline=True**, **field_equivalent=True**, **minimal_diff=True**\n  (only cell#0 source + metadata.cost differ; the rest is structurally identical).\n- **`detect_markdown_rendering`**: 0 violations (`frontmatter_rawyaml` resolved).\n- **`check_cost_metadata`**: 0 findings, `cost_source=metadata` canonical,\n  `notes` preserved.\n- **`_cost_equivalent`**: cell#0 no longer has a frontmatter → no divergence.\n- **`notebook_tools validate`**: 0 errors (1 warning **PRE-EXISTING** on\n  `origin/main`, unchanged by this edit — markdown-only cell#0 + metadata.cost\n  touched, no code cell affected).\n- nbformat 4.5, 65 cells unchanged, cell#0 `source` list format preserved.\n- Diff **+4/-19**, 1 file; catalogue byte-identical to main.\n\n## NOT `Closes #8955` (G.9 — would close an issue still open)\n\nFirsthand measure on this branch (`_cost_equivalent` over all notebooks) finds\n**10 ML-* quantbooks STILL cost-divergent** — `ML-Classification`,\n`ML-DeepLearning`, `ML-EnhancedPairs`, `ML-Ensemble`, `ML-FeatureEngineering`,\n`ML-RandomForest`, `ML-Regression`, `ML-SVM`, `ML-TextClassification`,\n`ML-XGBoost` (all `[cpu_min, reduced_pedagogical, reproducibility]`).\n\nThese are the turf of **#8908 (jsboige, OPEN, CHANGES_REQUESTED)** — ai-01 AND\nthe author himself have already identified the strip-only defect there\n(`No markdown content loss` FAILURE per notebook: stripping the frontmatter\nloses the curated cost values, the SAME regression class as my reverted\n#8959/#8963 and the subject of issue #8955 itself). The author has designated\n#8908 the **consolidation vehicle for the 33 QC** notebooks. They are reusable\nvia `migrate_cost_frontmatter_to_metadata.py --project ML-*` (#8966 script)\nshould the migration be folded into #8908. **This PR resolves hmm_alpha (the 1\nnon-QC divergent) only** — it does not touch the ML-* (active turf, #8908).\n\nSee #8955, #8904, #8056, #8966.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude-Code <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/8973/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/8973/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/9146","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/9146/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/9146/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsboige/CoursIA/issues/9146/events","html_url":"https://github.com/jsboige/CoursIA/pull/9146","id":5036448616,"node_id":"PR_kwDOH2Odns75Wf-x","number":9146,"title":"fix(search,#8052): CSP-7-Soft C# twin honest Verdict SOTA (parité cellule-à-cellule -> conceptuelle)","user":{"login":"jsboige","id":3159389,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNTkzODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3159389?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige","html_url":"https://github.com/jsboige","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jsboige/repos","events_url":"htt